Package: geoCensor
Title: Censoring-Aware Analysis of USGS National Geochemical Database Data
Version: 1.2.0.9006
Authors@R: person("Ross", "Edwards", email = "pedwards5@wisc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Ross Edwards [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Ross Edwards <pedwards5@wisc.edu>
Description: Tools to parse, model, and visualise left- and right-censored
    element concentrations from the U.S. Geological Survey National Geochemical
    Database (NGDB) and similar geochemical datasets. Functions parse USGS
    qvalue/qualifier detection-limit encodings into interval-censored fields,
    estimate censoring-aware maximum-likelihood lognormal geometric means
    (by state, via interval-censored survival regression) with confidence
    intervals, provide substitution-based alternatives for comparison, join
    chemistry to sample metadata, compute robust (bootstrap) Spearman
    correlations, run robust log10 principal component analysis, audit sampling
    support and observation counts, evaluate cell-declustering sensitivity, and produce
    ranked-bar and choropleth maps of state-level geometric means.
